  },
  {
   "type": "p",
   "text": "Use the style attribute with the\nwidth or height\nproperties to specify the size of a table, row or column."
  },
  {
   "type": "h2",
   "text": "HTML Table Width"
  },
  {
   "type": "p",
   "text": "To set the width of a table, add the style\nattribute to the <table> element:"
  },
  {
   "type": "code",
   "lang": "html",
   "text": "<table style=\"width:100%\">\n\n<tr>\n    <th>Firstname</th>\n\n    <th>Lastname</th>\n    <th>Age</th>\n\n</tr>\n\n<tr>\n    <td>Jill</td>\n\n    <td>Smith</td>\n    <td>50</td>\n\n</tr>\n  <tr>\n    <td>Eve</td>\n\n    <td>Jackson</td>\n    <td>94</td>\n\n  </tr>\n</table>",
   "caption": "Example"
  },
  {
   "type": "tryit",
   "url": "https://www.w3schools.com/tryit.asp?filename=tryhtml_table_width"
  },
  {
   "type": "note",
   "variant": "note",
   "text": "Using a percentage as the size unit for a width means\nhow wide will this element be compared to its parent element, which in this case\nis the <body>\nelement."
  },
  {
   "type": "h2",
   "text": "HTML Table Column Width"
  },
  {
